WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.634
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.400
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.501
Well, guys, today,
the C.E.O. of Pfizer said that

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:14.267
its vaccine for the Omicron
variant will be ready in March.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.901
So get ready for the craziest
St. Patrick's Day

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.334
in the history of the world.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.467
[ Irish accent ] Omicron.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:23.934
[ Normal voice ] Pretty soon,
the C.E.O. of Pfizer

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.567
is going to be on
Instagram Live like,

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.634
"New vaccine just dropped.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:30.067
Sound off in the comments!
What?!"

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.601
It feels like this
March Madness,

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.400
we'll be filling out brackets
to predict

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.033
which of the 68 variants
become the dominant strain.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.400
Listen to this.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.968
According to the CDC,
only 1 in 10 adults in the U.S.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.934
eat enough
fruits and vegetables.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.834
Good timing on this news, CDC.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.067
It sort of feels like
their version of

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.067
"Hey, what's over there?"

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.167
"There's a bird.
Look, there's a bird."

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.968
Yep, the CDC says adults
should eat 2 to 3 cups

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.701
of vegetables a day.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.667
Wait. Now they're saying 4 to 5.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.033
No, wait.
No, now they're saying only 1.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:04.968
Basically, barely 1 or 2.
You're fine with 1.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.000
Yeah, we'll figure it out.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.334
I heard that Tesla's
self-driving program

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.167
now offers three different modes
that control behaviors,

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.734
like rolling stops,
running yellow lights,

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.968
and how close you are
to follow other drivers.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.167
And they have three modes.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.467
They're called Chill, Average,
and Assertive.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.367
And this is fun.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:28.300
You can also hit Mood Swing and
try all three at random.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.167
And I also heard that some
Honda and Acura models

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.267
have been hit with a bug
that resets their clocks

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.734
20 years in the past.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.434
The company
could tell something was up

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.601
when drivers seemed happy.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.501
It's crazy.
People were driving along.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:47.634
Then, all of a sudden,

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.667
the radio would only play
the Goo Goo Dolls.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.267
Yeah. Get this.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:55.267
I saw that nearly 15,000 pounds
of Walmart beef sticks

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.501
have been recalled
because they forgot to label

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.567
a potential allergen.

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.234
Yep, Walmart beef sticks
must now have a label

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:05.868
that says "Warning -- you're
eating Walmart beef sticks."

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.634
Oh.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:10.767
-Oh. Oh, okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.434
Apparently, a supermarket chain
in the U.K. is getting rid of

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.901
the "use by" dates on its milk

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:19.167
and encouraging customers
to use the sniff test.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.234
Yep, here's how it works
in every house.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.801
You grab a carton
and immediately go,

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.767
"Honey, does
this smell bad to you?"

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.601
And, finally, a farmer in Turkey
is having his cows

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:34.033
wear V.R. goggles
that simulate green pastures

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.033
so that
they'll be less anxious.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.033
Take a look at this.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:40.067
It's real.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.701
Yeah, the cow doesn't make
any more milk,

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.501
but it is really good at
the new game "Beef Saber."

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.133
We have a great show, everybody.
Give it up for The Roots!

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.133
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:09.133
-Thank you very much, everybody.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:10.601
Some sad news last night.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:13.334
We heard that our friend
Bob Saget passed away.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.167
He was a great guest
on our show.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:17.033
Funny, funny, funny guy

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:19.267
and one of the nicest people
you could ever meet.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.801
Our thoughts go out
to his family.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.300
We're going to miss you, Bob.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.467
[ Applause ]

